      "writtenOn": "2025-02-06T21:23:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You want this data structure to have no alignment requirement, because you\u0027re converting a `\u0026[RMemHeader]` directly from possibly-unaligned bytes. `derive(Unaligned)` checks this at compile time.\n\nThe idiomatic way to do this is to dealign the integer types with `use zerocopy::byteorder::{U32, LE};` and replacing all of these `u32` fields with `U32\u003cLE\u003e` (or `zerocopy::byteorder::little_endian::U32` etc.).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 21,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "7e992e97ad1a98faaa388a202a90a03334bbe33f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d4e42302_9c7a8fdf",
        "filename": "guest/pvmfw/src/reserved_mem.rs",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 21,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-12T15:45:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe making the code agnostic of the CPU endianness is particularly relevant if you expect this code to run on both AArch64 and x86_64, which use different ones, AFAIU.",
      "parentUuid": "1d2b004c_10d0ee46",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 21,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "7e992e97ad1a98faaa388a202a90a03334bbe33f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
