      "lineNbr": 52,
      "author": {
        "id": 3562310
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-06T21:23:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Technically you can [check at compile time](https://docs.rs/zerocopy/latest/zerocopy/error/struct.SizeError.html#impl-From%3CConvertError%3CAlignmentError%3CSrc,+Dst%3E,+SizeError%3CSrc,+Dst%3E,+Infallible%3E%3E-for-SizeError%3CSrc,+Dst%3E) that `RMemHeader` is unaligned and that only a size error can occur:\n\n```suggestion\n        let (hdrs, buffer) \u003d \u003c[RMemHeader]\u003e::ref_from_prefix_with_elems(rem, count as usize)\n            .map_err(|e| { let _ \u003d SizeError::from(e); Error::InconsistentSize })?;\n```\n\nI\u0027m very open to syntax suggestions on making this check more ergonomic.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 51,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 52,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "7e992e97ad1a98faaa388a202a90a03334bbe33f",
