      "key": {
        "uuid": "36ca9f2e_8ac6a0ad",
        "filename": "guest/pvmfw/src/reserved_mem.rs",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 68,
      "author": {
        "id": 3562310
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-06T21:23:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this required by the overall header format or by our code?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 68,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 68,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "7e992e97ad1a98faaa388a202a90a03334bbe33f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "13d392a7_13721f8c",
        "filename": "guest/pvmfw/src/reserved_mem.rs",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 68,
      "author": {
        "id": 3562310
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-07T00:56:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If this is following the requirements of `\u0026CStr`, then this should check that _only_ the last byte is nul. I suggest using [`CStr::from_bytes_with_nul`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/ffi/struct.CStr.html#method.from_bytes_with_nul) and checking if it returns `Err`",
      "parentUuid": "36ca9f2e_8ac6a0ad",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 68,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 68,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "7e992e97ad1a98faaa388a202a90a03334bbe33f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d6aa6da8_d3d754b2",
        "filename": "guest/pvmfw/src/reserved_mem.rs",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 68,
      "author": {
        "id": 3562310
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-07T00:56:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit: Rust uses the term `nul` for the `\\0` terminator at the end of a `CStr`. It\u0027s _technically_ distinct from `null`, the pointer with address 0. Everyone knows what \"null terminator\" or \"null byte\" means though, so nbd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 68,
        "startChar": 48,
        "endLine": 68,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "7e992e97ad1a98faaa388a202a90a03334bbe33f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "92a64830_8a06d65c",
        "filename": "guest/pvmfw/src/reserved_mem.rs",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 68,
      "author": {
        "id": 1339975
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-08T00:57:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The header format doesn\u0027t specify a size for the compat string. Hypothetically we could derive it from either the next blob offset or the end of the buffer but that assumes both of those are correct.\n\nCurrently depthcharge sends null terminated strings. Since the primary documentation will live here, I can specify it when I add the README updates.\n\nAlso, I updated this to parse the `CStr`.",
      "parentUuid": "36ca9f2e_8ac6a0ad",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 68,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 68,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "7e992e97ad1a98faaa388a202a90a03334bbe33f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2ae59832_831c286d",
        "filename": "guest/pvmfw/src/reserved_mem.rs",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 83,
      "author": {
        "id": 3562310
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-06T21:23:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is an unnecessary double reference (which is hinted at by the ignored lifetime). Instead, `derive(Clone, Copy)` on `ConfigHeader\u003c\u0027a\u003e` and have that be directly `IntoIterator`. Also, `hdr: ConfigHeader\u003c\u0027a\u003e`.\n\n```suggestion\nimpl\u003c\u0027a\u003e IntoIterator for ConfigHeader\u003c\u0027a\u003e {\n```",
      "revId": "7e992e97ad1a98faaa388a202a90a03334bbe33f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b84720ae_6bb86e22",
        "filename": "guest/pvmfw/src/reserved_mem.rs",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 83,
      "author": {
        "id": 1339975
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-08T00:57:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Isn\u0027t it needed since `into_iter` takes `self` and not `\u0026self`?",
      "parentUuid": "2ae59832_831c286d",
      "revId": "7e992e97ad1a98faaa388a202a90a03334bbe33f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ced9b10d_728d71a0",
        "filename": "guest/pvmfw/src/reserved_mem.rs",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 83,
      "author": {
        "id": 3562310
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-10T20:25:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, if you make `ConfigHeader: Copy` as I say then `into_iter` won\u0027t consume the original object, but copy it. This is true for all `Copy` types - calling a `self` method does a copy and not a move. It\u0027s like how calling `.into_iter()` on a `\u0026Vec\u003cT\u003e` yields an `impl Iterator\u003cItem \u003d \u0026T\u003e` by copying the reference (though `.iter()` is preferred when it\u0027s there).\n\nIf a type consists of just `\u0026T`, there\u0027s rarely a reason to prevent it from being `Clone` at least.",
      "parentUuid": "b84720ae_6bb86e22",
      "revId": "7e992e97ad1a98faaa388a202a90a03334bbe33f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cf908eb1_90de9393",
        "filename": "guest/pvmfw/src/reserved_mem.rs",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 83,
      "author": {
        "id": 1339975
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-12T01:48:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done",
      "parentUuid": "ced9b10d_728d71a0",
      "revId": "7e992e97ad1a98faaa388a202a90a03334bbe33f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4689e779_a759e335",
        "filename": "guest/pvmfw/src/reserved_mem.rs",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 104,
      "author": {
        "id": 3562310
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-06T21:23:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is emitting the _entire_ `buffer` for each iteration. I would instead expect it to yield the portion of the `buffer` that is specifically relevant to the current `\u0026\u0027a RMemHeader`. That way the user of the iterator doesn\u0027t need to do any offset calculations.\n\nOtherwise the iterator doesn\u0027t provide much value: it\u0027d be more clear to have `fn headers(\u0026self) -\u003e \u0026[RMemHeader]` and `fn buffer(\u0026self) -\u003e \u0026[u8]` getters and have the user `for` loop over the headers.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 104,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 104,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "7e992e97ad1a98faaa388a202a90a03334bbe33f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
