      "message": "Please test that intentionally dealigned input data is not rejected:\n\n```rust\n/// Ensure `data` is aligned on an odd address; output the original data.\n/// Resizes `data` if necessary.\nfn dealign_vec_data(data: \u0026mut Vec\u003cu8\u003e) -\u003e \u0026[u8] {\n    assert!(data.len() \u003e\u003d 4);\n    data.reserve(1);\n    let out \u003d if data.as_ptr() as usize % 2 \u003d\u003d 0 {\n        data.insert(0, 0);\n        \u0026data[1..]\n    } else {\n        \u0026data\n    };\n    assert!(matches!(u16::ref_from_prefix(out), Err(error::ConvertError::Alignment(_))));\n    out\n}\n```\n\nUsing this on `bytes` and passing to `ConfigHeader::new` should currently fail with an erroneous `InconsistentSize` while trying to read the header slice.",
